### 28. Explain the category prediction flow.

**Interview-ready answer:**  

```python
inputs = tokenizer(
    text,
    return_tensors="pt",
    truncation=True,
    padding=True,
    max_length=512,
)
output = category_model(**inputs)
probabilities = torch.softmax(output.logits, dim=1)
class_id = torch.argmax(probabilities, dim=1).item()
category = label_encoder.inverse_transform([class_id])[0]
```

The model returns logits. Softmax converts them to a probability distribution. The highest-probability class is selected and mapped back to a human-readable label.

**Technical concept:**  
Logits are unnormalized model scores; softmax converts them into values that sum to one.

---

